Definitely.  Easy proof:

 1. If the wish isn't green DSM, tin of green dragon meat, or a couple of
other less pareto-efficient things, the RNG can instakill you with
various poisoned traps.

 2. Most ordinary players would not feel confident of winning the game
with merely Green DSM or early intrinsic PR as an advantage.

So there's no perfect wish.

I wonder if you could identity super-duper-ooper nethack players by
offering the choice of free Green, Yellow, Grey or Silver DSM at the start
of a game.  Only the really confident ones would take protection against
rare but *unfair* death over the other options.

